Write one short markdown memo for the team lead from the single notes file /private/tmp/hirearchy-e6-s3-1792861552/notes/2026-10-19.md (read-only; do not edit it). Save it as lead/writer/work/memo-2026-10-19.md. Layout: first line 'Summary: ...' (one line), then a 'Decisions' section, then an 'Action items' section (a table). No other sections (no 'Open questions' or 'Open, not decided' section). Decisions = firm decisions only; discussed-but-open items are not decisions. Due rules: ISO date when the notes make it clear (explicit dates in the notes; 'ACTION ... by Oct 23' means 2026-10-23), otherwise 'none'. Vague/hedged deadlines (e.g. 'probably by end of next week', 'during that first week') with no clear date -> none. Include every commitment, including informal prose ones ('X said he'd ...', 'X offered to ...', 'X will ...') as well as the ACTION-labelled ones. Tell me in your report which rows came from informal prose. Use only what the notes state; invent nothing.

## Acceptance criteria
